\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces One trusted revision requires separate decisions about work and its use. [EL] confirms the complete frozen input of $j_3$ against actual selected $P_2$. [AU] retains original Correct/Update before durable selection; the call's own prediction can differ from its result. [SUP] independently retains the whole supported view when $P_2$ installs. Unknown input remains unresolved while owned calls may run or buffer; it grants no commit authority. Arrows show decisions and their outcomes; the dashed red branch marks failed support. This is a causal schematic without a measured time scale.}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
